        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Auty, Mary Plazas, Giacomo Puccini\n- Works: La Bohème (2009 film), La bohème, \"O soave fanciulla\"\n- Places: Ethiopia, Britain, continental Europe\n- Roles: operatic tenor\n\nFacts:\n- Peter Robert Auty was born on 4 November 1969.\n- Peter Auty is an English operatic tenor.\n- Peter Auty has worked with most major opera companies in Britain and with a number of companies in continental Europe.\n- The 2009 four-minute film La Bohème features images of harsh life in Ethiopia.\n- La Bohème is set to the duet \"O soave fanciulla\" from Giacomo Puccini's opera La bohème.\n- Peter Auty and Mary Plazas sang the duet used in La Bohème.",
